To Whom It May Concern:

Pursuant to the California Public Records Act (CPRA), California Government Code
§ 6250 et seq., we hereby request copies of or access to the following public records:

RECORDS REQUESTED:

    1.  All video recordings, still images, or digital data captured by any
        traffic-control or intersection-monitoring camera located at or near:

                {{ incident_location }}

        on {{ incident_date }}, for the time period of 7:00 AM through 8:30 AM
        (or the full available recording period encompassing that window).

    2.  All traffic signal timing records, event logs, or fault logs for the
        signal system at the above intersection on {{ incident_date }}.

    3.  A log or inventory of any traffic cameras operating at or within 500 feet
        of the above intersection on {{ incident_date }}, including the name of
        the agency maintaining each camera and the standard retention period for
        recordings.

EVIDENCE PRESERVATION DEMAND:

Because traffic camera recordings are subject to automatic overwrite cycles, we
demand that any records responsive to this request be immediately preserved and
placed on litigation hold, regardless of any scheduled deletion or overwrite. Failure
to preserve these records after receipt of this letter may constitute spoliation of
evidence in anticipated civil litigation.

RESPONSE REQUESTED:

Pursuant to Government Code § 6253(c), please respond within ten (10) days of
receipt of this request. If any portion of this request is denied, please identify
the specific statutory exemption relied upon for each denial.

If records cannot be produced within ten days, please provide an estimated date of
production as required by Government Code § 6253(c)(1).

